---
title: Creamy Cilantro Jalapeño Sauce
description: Smooth, spicy blender sauce with fresh cilantro and jalapeño. Ideal for tacos, grilled meats, quesadillas, or dipping vegetables.
image: https://www.thecomfortofcooking.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/08/110.jpg
tags: sauce, condiment, dip, vegan, mexican, quick, gluten-free
time required: 5 minutes
servings: 4
author: Georgia Johnson
source: https://www.thecomfortofcooking.com/creamy-cilantro-jalapeno-sauce
---

Combine @jalapeños{4%medium}(halved and deseeded), @cilantro{1½%cups}(loosely packed), @vegan mayo{½%cup}, @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @salt{=¼%tsp}, and the juice of @lime{1} in a #food processor{} and process until smooth.

If you desire a thicker texture, add more vegan mayo. If you desire a thinner texture, add @olive oil{1%tsp}(at a time) until you reach the desired consistency.

> Store refrigerated up to 5 days.
